---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Donor Disclosures | Fuzhou America"
  description="Tax-exempt status, New York State charities registration, and financial report availability for Fuzhou America Inc."
  current="disclosures"
>
  <header class="intro-header cc-subpage">
    <h1 class="heading-jumbo">Donor Disclosures</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Tax-Exempt Status</h2>
      <p>
        Fuzhou America Inc. is a New York not-for-profit corporation recognized by the IRS as a 501(c)(3) public
        charity (EIN 83-4182352). Contributions are tax-deductible to the extent allowed by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-heading">New York State Registration</h2>
      <p>
        Fuzhou America Inc. is registered with the New York State Attorney General's Charities Bureau
        (NYS Reg. No. 51-78-72).
      </p>
      <p>Fuzhou America Inc. will file its first annual financial report with the NYS Attorney General by May 15, 2027. Once filed, it will be posted at <a href="https://www.charitiesnys.com">www.charitiesnys.com</a>, where you can also find information on charities (or call the Attorney General at <span style="white-space: nowrap;">(212) 416-8686</span>). The report and a description of our programs are available on request from 43-28 158th St, Unit B, Flushing, NY 11358.</p>

      <h2 class="section-heading">Fiscally Sponsored Projects</h2>
      <p>
        Fuzhou America Inc. acts as fiscal sponsor for charitable, educational and cultural projects that advance its
        purposes. Contributions made for a sponsored project are received by Fuzhou America Inc. and remain subject to
        its discretion and control.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-heading">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:info@fuzhouamerica.org">info@fuzhouamerica.org</a>. We answer requests for our financial
        report within 15 days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
